 ## Overview
-CSG Model Voxelization is a hardware-accelerated algorithm that generates a binary voxelization of a Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) model by encoding primitive classifications into frame buffer pixel colors and using logical operations to compute the final CSG classification implicitly via the Point-Classification Map (PCM) [S1]. It differs from [SDF-based Voxelization](6595-sdf-based-voxelization.md) by operating in image space via rasterization rather than distance field evaluation, and from [Sequential CSG](7629-sequential-csg.md) by leveraging GPU blending and logical operations for parallel boolean combination rather than linear CPU iteration [S1].
+CSG Model Voxelization is a hardware-accelerated algorithm that generates a binary voxelization of a Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) model by encoding primitive classifications into frame buffer pixel colors and using logical operations to compute the final CSG classification implicitly via the Point-Classification Map (PCM) [S1]. It differs from [SDF-based Voxelization](6595-sdf-based-voxelization.md) by operating in image space via rasterization rather than distance field evaluation, and from [Sequential CSG](7629-sequential-csg.md) by leveraging GPU blending and logical operations for parallel boolean combination rather than linear CPU iteration [S1]. The method implements set operations (union, intersection, difference) by mapping them to bitwise logical operations on framebuffers [S2].
 
